n levels in leaves, leaf exudate and shoot apical meristem of <italic>Arabidopsis thaliana</italic> during floral transition</article-title><source>Journal of Experimental Botany</source><year>2003</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>2511</fpage><lpage>2517</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14512385</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crawford</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nitrate: nutrient and signal</article-title><source>The Plant Cell</source><year>1995</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>859</fpage><lpage>868</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7640524</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Photosynthetic acclimation and nitrogen partitioning within a lucerne canopy. I Canopy characteristics</article-title><source>Australian Journal of Plant Physiology</source><year>1993</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>55</fpage><lpage>67</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Seemann</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Briggs</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The allocation of protein nitrogen in the photosynthetic apparatus: costs, consequences, and control</article-title><source>Photosynthesis</source><year>1989</year><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Liss</publisher-name><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>205</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franklin</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><